    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103769" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τήθη</span></b>  (sts. written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηθή</span>; the 
			Ion.
		 voc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆθα</span>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
			Il.
			3.130
		</span></i>, prob. belongs to this word), ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>grandmother</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				49
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lys.</u>
				549
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.128
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				461d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				3.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1534.229
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				57.20
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιτθῆς, -ῇ</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				532.4
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιθή</span> codd.), Hierocl.<i><span class="en">
				p.61
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιτθαί, τίθαι, τίτθαι</span>
			codd.), <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Or.</u>
				25.47
			</span></i> (vv. ll. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τήτθη, τίθη</span>),
				Thom.Mag.<i><span class="en">
				p.359
			</span></i> R. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίθη</span> codd. and prob. <i><span class="en">
				Thom.
			</span></i>); title of play by Diphilus, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.2363.35
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίθη λέγεται ἡ μάμμη, τίτθη ἡ
				βυζάστρια, τιθήνη ἡ τροφός</span> Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
			</span></i>Gr. post Moer.<i><span class="en">
				p.479
			</span></i> P., cf. Ptol.Asc.<i><span class="en">
				p.394
			</span></i> H., etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>nurse</i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆ, ὅθεν καὶ τήθη ἡ
				λέγουσα "δέξαι, θήλασον</span>" Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.219
			</span></i>, cf. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				549
			</span></i>; but this is an error, the word for <i>nurse</i> being
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίτθη</span> (q.v.).</div>
